Subject: [PATCH 1/4] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's patch 1, built on
 ea41e6fc9): A GATE THAT NEEDS GIT IS REFUSED WHERE THERE IS NONE (the seat's
 planted case PV9). On a git-archive export nine of the ten gates that need
 git passed: three answered 'skipped', and six asked git for the tracked
 files, were given none and found nothing wrong among none ('ok (0 tests, 0
 vacuous)'). What kind of tree a gate runs in is now read once
 (checkout_state: a clone, or an export -- an archive, a copy, a folder that
 merely sits inside another repository); a table names the nineteen gates that
 reach git, seven for the tracked files and twelve for the past or other
 seats' branches; and each gate of the table is replaced, in GATES and under
 its own name, by a gate that asks first whether it can look and is refused in
 plain words where it cannot. A gate stays one thing however it is reached, so
 main's rule that a test names the gate it controls holds as written; the
 thirty-four gates outside the table are left exactly as they were. The push
 hook's detached worktree is a clone and is not refused. THE TABLE IS HELD TO
 THE CODE: every gate not in it is run with git and without, and must answer
 the same word for word, so a new gate that calls git unlisted fails; a gate
 listed as reading the tracked files only may not call a git command that
 reads the past. TWO OF MAIN'S TESTS ARE RE-PINNED, each with a dated note:
 one read the words an export printed (three gates printed SKIP; they are
 printed FAIL with the refusal now), one drove views-generated by name on a
 folder with no repository (the folder is made a repository, so that the gate
 reaches the missing generator the test is about). The lock:
 tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py, seven tests; on the commit
 before, its first fails with the nine gates by name. Not in this commit: the
 generated views, which change when a test file is added. 0 of 19.

